course: dictionary
lesson: 212
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. Alexia is one of these. In medicine, alexia is a noun meaning a loss of the ability to read, usually after damage to the brain, for example from a stroke, in someone who could read before.
explain: Alexia is also a girl's name. Read this: «England's women's football team, the Lionesses, won the European Championship in 2022 and again in 2025; Sam Kerr and Alexia Putellas are among the world's best players.» Alexia comes before a person's surname, and it is a person, so it is a name.
explain: Look for clues. The capital A shows a name, and talk of people shows a name. Talk of a stroke, damage to the brain or reading loss shows the medical word. Always ask: is this sentence about a person, or about the brain and reading?
fact: Alexia is a noun meaning a loss of the ability to read after damage to the brain.
fact: Alexia can also be a girl's name, as in «Alexia Putellas» from the football sentence.
fact: Alexia usually comes from damage to the brain, for example from a stroke.
fact: Alexia is not the same as dyslexia: dyslexia is a difficulty with learning to read, while alexia is losing a reading ability someone already had.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Sam Kerr and Alexia Putellas are among the world's best players.» In this sentence, what is Alexia? | *A girl's name | A loss of the ability to read | A kind of brain scan | A football team
exercise: A doctor says a patient has alexia after a stroke. What does alexia mean here? | *A loss of the ability to read, after damage to the brain | A kind of hard test at school | A girl who is a fast reader | A football team that won a big prize
exercise: A story says, «Alexia came first in the class spelling test.» What does Alexia most likely mean? | *A girl's name | A brain scan for doctors | A note from the nurse | A loss of reading ability after a stroke
test: «After the accident, Mr Bell had alexia and could no longer read his post.» What does alexia mean? | *A loss of reading ability after damage to the brain | A name for a postman | Reading very quickly | A kind of car accident
test: Is alexia the same as dyslexia? | Yes, they are exactly the same | Yes, both are names for girls | *No, alexia is losing a reading ability you had, while dyslexia is a difficulty with learning to read | No, alexia is a football team
exam: Which is the best clue that Alexia is a name? | A noun with no person in it | A stroke and damage to the brain | The word alexia in a science book | *A capital A and a person doing something
